    "title": "Radiocarbon date, Sample number OxA-4742",
    "description": "Fabric, id as wool, TT/87/285, from Roman fort at Vindolanda / Chesterholm, Northumberland, England. Subm C R Cork, W D Cooke and J P Wild (UMIST). Comment (subm CRC): provenance is Room X of the Praetorium of Cerialis (Pd III), whence a number of unusual finds have been excavated. This one is an intricate fabric withseam- and hem-craftsmanship contrasting with some of the coarser stitchwork on other finds. Date shows it to have been at least 30 years old at the time of deposition, and probably imported.<br>",
